WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.255
Lesson 6.2.

00:00:02.255 --> 00:00:06.325
Tokenomics: supply, unlocks, FDV, value capture.

00:00:06.325 --> 00:00:08.535
By the end of this lesson, you'll be

00:00:08.535 --> 00:00:11.103
able to read a token's supply schedule and

00:00:11.103 --> 00:00:14.030
judge whether protocol success reaches the token.

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:16.620
Here's the plan.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.305
First, the key ideas.

00:00:18.305 --> 00:00:21.020
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:22.545
Then, your checklist.

00:00:22.545 --> 00:00:24.707
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:26.007 --> 00:00:29.482
First, Circulating supply: tokens tradable now.

00:00:29.482 --> 00:00:32.557
Max/total supply: all that will exist.

00:00:32.557 --> 00:00:35.902
Next, Market cap = price × circulating.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:41.242
FDV (fully diluted valuation) = price × max supply.

00:00:41.242 --> 00:00:45.340
Then, Unlocks/vesting: team and investor tokens released on

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:48.372
a schedule; new supply that may be sold.

00:00:48.372 --> 00:00:52.097
Also, Emissions: ongoing new tokens (rewards).

00:00:52.097 --> 00:00:55.445
And finally, Value capture: does protocol revenue

00:00:55.445 --> 00:00:58.927
actually reach token holders (fee share, buybacks),

00:00:58.927 --> 00:01:00.467
and how is it enforced?

00:01:01.767 --> 00:01:04.282
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:01:04.282 --> 00:01:08.683
Price $2, circulating 100M, max 1B:

00:01:08.683 --> 00:01:12.162
market cap $200M, FDV $2B.

00:01:12.162 --> 00:01:17.342
Next month 50M unlock: circulating supply rises 50%.

00:01:17.342 --> 00:01:20.952
Unless demand grows to match, that's heavy selling pressure.

00:01:20.952 --> 00:01:22.838
A low market cap with a

00:01:22.838 --> 00:01:24.567
huge FDV is a warning.

00:01:25.867 --> 00:01:27.327
Here's your checklist.

00:01:27.327 --> 00:01:28.862
Do it now, for real.

00:01:28.862 --> 00:01:32.407
First, Market cap vs FDV compared.

00:01:32.407 --> 00:01:35.232
Next, Next 12 months of unlocks listed.

00:01:35.232 --> 00:01:39.292
And finally, Value-capture mechanism identified (or "none").

00:01:40.592 --> 00:01:41.802
Question 1.

00:01:41.802 --> 00:01:46.042
Price $5, circulating 20M, max 100M.

00:01:46.042 --> 00:01:47.002
FDV?

00:01:51.422 --> 00:01:53.467
The answer: $500M.

00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:56.012
Question 2.

00:01:56.012 --> 00:01:57.397
Why do unlocks matter?

00:02:01.817 --> 00:02:04.887
The answer: They add supply that recipients may sell.

00:02:06.187 --> 00:02:07.457
Question 3.

00:02:07.457 --> 00:02:08.742
What is value capture?

00:02:13.162 --> 00:02:15.142
The answer: An enforceable way

00:02:15.142 --> 00:02:17.442
protocol success benefits the token.

00:02:18.742 --> 00:02:19.987
Let's recap.

00:02:19.987 --> 00:02:23.072
Circulating supply: tokens tradable now.

00:02:23.072 --> 00:02:25.927
Market cap = price × circulating.

00:02:25.927 --> 00:02:30.687
Unlocks/vesting: team and investor tokens released on a schedule.

00:02:30.687 --> 00:02:33.402
Emissions: ongoing new tokens (rewards).

00:02:34.702 --> 00:02:37.217
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:02:37.217 --> 00:02:40.837
Next up, Lesson 6.3: Governance & DAOs.
